*> Implementation test (002-lane-mobsa5; 05c 0x2A Player Command action 3 START_RIDING_JUMP, 19 section 3.1, 54 section 6.3): the riding jump through the real Player Command path. A saddled camel
*> under the rider dashes (cooldown 55); a saddled horse on the ground leaps with the vertical speed jump strength x scale (0.4 + 0.4 p / 90 below 90) and the forward impulse 0.4 x scale; strength 0,
*> no saddle and no mount do nothing; a new horse draws a jump strength of 0.4 to 1.0.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-MOB-44-RIDEJUMP.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY BRWORLD.
 COPY STDMOBS.
 01 WS-PLAYER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CONN                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-ENTITY-ROW          PIC X(66).
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TYPE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CAMEL               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HORSE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DIM                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X0                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Z0                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FLOOR               BINARY-LONG VALUE 40.
 01 WS-SIZE                BINARY-LONG VALUE 48.
 01 WS-STONE               BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-X                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Y                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-YAW                 FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ACTION              BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
 01 WS-DATA                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-OK                  BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "MS-TEST-OPEN" USING WS-PLAYER
     MOVE PL-CONN(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-CONN
     MOVE PL-DIM(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-DIM
     COMPUTE WS-X0 = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-X(WS-PLAYER)) - 24
     COMPUTE WS-Z0 = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Z(WS-PLAYER)) - 24
     CALL "MS-TEST-FLOOR" USING WS-DIM WS-X0 WS-Z0 WS-SIZE WS-FLOOR WS-STONE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE 2 TO BW-DIFFICULTY
     MOVE 6000 TO CW-TIME
     COMPUTE WS-Y = WS-FLOOR + 1
     COMPUTE WS-X = WS-X0 + 24.5
     COMPUTE WS-Z = WS-Z0 + 24.5
     MOVE "minecraft:camel" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-TYPE WS-ENTITY-ROW WS-STATUS
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-CAMEL
     MOVE "minecraft:horse" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-TYPE WS-ENTITY-ROW WS-STATUS
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW WS-HORSE
     MOVE 1 TO EN-ON-GROUND(WS-CAMEL) EN-ON-GROUND(WS-HORSE)
     MOVE "acceptance US15 19§3.2 Horse jump: a new horse draws a jump strength of 0.4 to 1.0" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF EN-HORSE-JUMP(WS-HORSE) >= 0.4 AND EN-HORSE-JUMP(WS-HORSE) <= 1.0
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   No mount: nothing happens (the call returns).
     MOVE 80 TO WS-DATA
     CALL "TEST-PLAYER-COMMAND-DATA" USING WS-CONN WS-ACTION WS-DATA
     MOVE "acceptance US15 54§6.3 Riding jump: a player without a mount jumps nothing" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-CAMEL-DASH(WS-CAMEL) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   A saddled camel under the rider: the dash starts.
     MOVE 1 TO EN-SADDLE(WS-CAMEL)
     MOVE 0 TO EN-CAMEL-POSE(WS-CAMEL) EN-CAMEL-POSE-T(WS-CAMEL)
     MOVE WS-CAMEL TO EN-VEHICLE(PL-ENTITY-ROW(WS-PLAYER))
     MOVE WS-PLAYER TO EN-RIDER(WS-CAMEL)
     MOVE 0 TO WS-DATA
     CALL "TEST-PLAYER-COMMAND-DATA" USING WS-CONN WS-ACTION WS-DATA
     MOVE "acceptance US15 54§6.3 Riding jump: a strength of 0 starts nothing" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-CAMEL-DASH(WS-CAMEL) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 80 TO WS-DATA
     CALL "TEST-PLAYER-COMMAND-DATA" USING WS-CONN WS-ACTION WS-DATA
     MOVE "acceptance US15 54§6.3 Riding jump: the camel dashes with its cooldown 55" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 55 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-CAMEL-DASH(WS-CAMEL) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO EN-RIDER(WS-CAMEL)

*>   A saddled horse: strength 90 (full scale 1.0) gives vertical speed = the jump strength and the forward impulse 0.4.
     MOVE WS-HORSE TO EN-VEHICLE(PL-ENTITY-ROW(WS-PLAYER))
     MOVE WS-PLAYER TO EN-RIDER(WS-HORSE)
     MOVE 0.8 TO EN-HORSE-JUMP(WS-HORSE)
     MOVE 90 TO WS-DATA
     CALL "TEST-PLAYER-COMMAND-DATA" USING WS-CONN WS-ACTION WS-DATA
     MOVE "acceptance US15 19§3.1 Riding jump: an unsaddled horse does not jump" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-VY(WS-HORSE) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO EN-SADDLE(WS-HORSE)
     CALL "TEST-PLAYER-COMMAND-DATA" USING WS-CONN WS-ACTION WS-DATA
     MOVE "acceptance US15 19§3.1 Riding jump: a saddled horse leaps with vertical speed 0.8 x 1.0 and forward 0.4" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF EN-VY(WS-HORSE) > 0.79 AND EN-VY(WS-HORSE) < 0.81 AND EN-VZ(WS-HORSE) > 0.39 AND EN-VZ(WS-HORSE) < 0.41 AND EN-ON-GROUND(WS-HORSE) = 0
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO EN-ON-GROUND(WS-HORSE)
     MOVE 0 TO EN-VY(WS-HORSE) EN-VZ(WS-HORSE)
     MOVE 45 TO WS-DATA
     CALL "TEST-PLAYER-COMMAND-DATA" USING WS-CONN WS-ACTION WS-DATA
     MOVE "acceptance US15 19§3.1 Riding jump: strength 45 gives the scale 0.6" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF EN-VY(WS-HORSE) > 0.47 AND EN-VY(WS-HORSE) < 0.49 AND EN-VZ(WS-HORSE) > 0.23 AND EN-VZ(WS-HORSE) < 0.25
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   In the air: no second jump; a horse without a drawn strength jumps with 0.7.
     MOVE 0 TO EN-VY(WS-HORSE)
     CALL "TEST-PLAYER-COMMAND-DATA" USING WS-CONN WS-ACTION WS-DATA
     MOVE "acceptance US15 19§3.1 Riding jump: a horse in the air does not jump again" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-VY(WS-HORSE) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO EN-ON-GROUND(WS-HORSE)
     MOVE 0 TO EN-HORSE-JUMP(WS-HORSE)
     MOVE 90 TO WS-DATA
     CALL "TEST-PLAYER-COMMAND-DATA" USING WS-CONN WS-ACTION WS-DATA
     MOVE "acceptance US15 19§3.1 Riding jump: a horse without a drawn strength jumps with 0.7" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 0 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     IF EN-VY(WS-HORSE) > 0.69 AND EN-VY(WS-HORSE) < 0.71
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-MOB-44-RIDEJUMP.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-PLAYER-COMMAND-DATA.
*> USING connection id, action, data: feeds Player Command (05c 0x2A) with the player's own entity id and that data.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 64.
 01 WS-PACKET-ID           BINARY-LONG VALUE 42.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-ID                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-ACTION               BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-DATA                 BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-ID L-ACTION L-DATA.
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-PACKET-ID
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER PL-ENTITY-ID(CN-PLAYER(L-ID))
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-ACTION
     CALL "PB-PUT-VARINT" USING PB-BUFFER L-DATA
     CALL "TEST-FEED-BUFFER" USING L-ID PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM TEST-PLAYER-COMMAND-DATA.
 COPY CORETEST.
 COPY MOBSPTEST.
